abstract={We aimed to measure the internal recycling of nitrogen between the animal host and symbiotic algae in the hermatypic coral Stylophora pistillata , a dominant reef builder at Elat. Using data of excretion rate of the animal nitrogen content of both partners and nitrogen required for their growth, we constructed a model of nitrogen flux and recycling between zooxanthellae and animal host in S. pistillata . Our model shows that nitrogen excreted from the animal and taken up by the algae is used efficiently and serves as a mechanism of nitrogen conservation within the association. Nevertheless, external nitrogen sources such as dissolved inorganic/organic N and particulate organic N are needed for activities such as growth, reproduction, etc.},
