month={NA},
abstract={Proceeding from the assumption that sea water in the vicinity of seashore colonies of birds is fertilized with excreta of birds, the author analyses the changes occurring in marine phytoplankton. The effect of the enrichment of water with nutrient, due to guano dissolution, on the growth of planktonic test-objects Skeletonema costatum and Nitzschia seriata has been verified experimentally. Natural observations show that an increase in the enrichment of water with birds' excreta observed from time to time favours an unusually intensive development of phytoplankton. During summer the changes in nutrient salt concentration and phytoplankton number near the seashore colonies of birds are of a correlative pulsating character. The original materials are used to draw a conclusion about the importance of the areas with stable biological productivity which are created near sea-shore colonies of birds as specific agents affecting the productivity of the near-shore zone of the sea..},
